Subject: [LOCAL CANDIDATE] wifi: ath10k: skip unacknowledged WCN3990 pairwise key deletion wait

Base: linux-v6.17.0-sm8150, matching the cached postmarketOS
6.17.0-r2 source archive.
Based on David Heidelberg's RFC discussion:
https://lkml.rescloud.iu.edu/hypermail/linux/kernel/2609.2/06093.html

This local variant enables the quirk for WCN3990 only. Other hardware,
SET_KEY,
group-key operations and transport errors retain their existing
handling.
WMI_KEY_PAIRWISE is zero; pairwise is selected by absence of
WMI_KEY_GROUP.

Validated by cross-compilation and isolated tests of the actual C
function.
Not yet validated with this firmware on device; not installed on the
phone.
No upstream acceptance or sign-off is asserted.
---
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/hw.h b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/hw.h
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/hw.h
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/hw.h
@@ -638,6 +638,9 @@
 
 	/* The hardware support multicast frame registrations */
 	bool mcast_frame_registration;
+
+	/* WCN3990 does not acknowledge pairwise key removal over HTT. */
+	bool no_pairwise_key_del_ind;
 };
 
 struct htt_resp;
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/core.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/core.c
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/core.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/core.c
@@ -716,6 +716,7 @@
 		.dev_id = 0,
 		.bus = ATH10K_BUS_SNOC,
 		.name = "wcn3990 hw1.0",
+		.no_pairwise_key_del_ind = true,
 		.led_pin = 0,
 		.continuous_frag_desc = true,
 		.tx_chain_mask = 0x7,
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/mac.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/mac.c
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/mac.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/mac.c
@@ -316,6 +316,14 @@
 	ret = ath10k_send_key(arvif, key, cmd, macaddr, flags);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
+
+	/* WCN3990 sends no security indication for a pairwise key deletion.
+	 * Keep waiting for installations and group-key changes: those do
+	 * generate indications and must retain their timeout protection.
+	 */
+	if (cmd == DISABLE_KEY && !(flags & WMI_KEY_GROUP) &&
+	    ar->hw_params.no_pairwise_key_del_ind)
+		return 0;
 
 	time_left = wait_for_completion_timeout(&ar->install_key_done, 3 * HZ);
 	if (time_left == 0)
